1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,450
Come and be a scale, like mine!

2
00:00:02,498 --> 00:00:03,488
Shrink down.

3
00:00:03,768 --> 00:00:04,698
Quietly.

4
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:10,057
You are one tiny scale, on a lizard's back.

5
00:00:10,722 --> 00:00:11,762
You are dry.

6
00:00:12,172 --> 00:00:13,992
Not moist, like the frog.

7
00:00:14,382 --> 00:00:16,212
All around you, more scales.

8
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:18,235
It is early morning.

9
00:00:18,665 --> 00:00:19,995
The shade is cool.

10
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:22,205
So the lizard is cool too.

11
00:00:22,793 --> 00:00:24,493
Now it crawls into the sun.

12
00:00:25,901 --> 00:00:27,191
The rock is warm.

13
00:00:27,611 --> 00:00:28,571
You warm up.

14
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:30,811
The whole lizard warms up!

15
00:00:31,618 --> 00:00:33,228
A cloud hides the sun.

16
00:00:33,628 --> 00:00:35,118
You cool down again.

17
00:00:38,024 --> 00:00:40,454
Reptiles are cold-blooded animals.

18
00:00:40,884 --> 00:00:44,554
This means that they do not have a constant body temperature like

19
00:00:44,304 --> 00:00:45,104
humans.

20
00:00:45,524 --> 00:00:49,814
Their body temperature changes with the environment that they are in.

21
00:00:52,799 --> 00:00:54,099
Dry, scaly skin.

22
00:00:54,199 --> 00:00:55,239
Cold-blooded.

23
00:00:55,289 --> 00:00:56,259
That is me!

24
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:57,619
I am a reptile!
